From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:11:01 +0200
Subject: fix: deliver clicks that another process posts to a background app

-[RenderWidgetHostViewCocoa acceptsFirstMouse:] returns NO by default so that
the click which activates a window is not also delivered to the page. AppKit
asks the same question for a mouse down that another process posted directly
to this process, for example with CGEventPostToPid(). Such an event does not go
through the window server, so it activates nothing, and answering NO drops it.

AppKit activates the app before it asks about a click that the window server
routed here, so an inactive app at this point identifies the posted event.
Hardware events have no source process, and events this process posts carry
its own, so both keep the existing behavior. A window that ignores mouse events
never gets a routed click, so it does not take a posted one either.

Landed upstream as https://crrev.com/c/8470994 (r1715473) without the
ignoresMouseEvents check, which follows in a separate CL; this patch can be
removed once both have rolled in.

diff --git a/content/app_shim_remote_cocoa/render_widget_host_view_cocoa.mm b/content/app_shim_remote_cocoa/render_widget_host_view_cocoa.mm
index fdd3f750a8e56b96b363ca6e0155cfef7ee44907..ddc0d6649c9fe7df611b390c27f1f9f2ee72ab86 100644
--- a/content/app_shim_remote_cocoa/render_widget_host_view_cocoa.mm
+++ b/content/app_shim_remote_cocoa/render_widget_host_view_cocoa.mm
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <AppKit/AppKit.h>
 #include <Carbon/Carbon.h>  // for <HIToolbox/Events.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <limits>
@@ -876,6 +877,20 @@ - (BOOL)acceptsFirstMouse:(NSEvent*)theEvent {
       [self.window acceptsFirstMouse])
     return YES;
 
+  // A click that another process posts straight to this process does not
+  // activate the app, unlike one the window server routes here, so treating it
+  // as an activation click would only drop it. The window server never routes
+  // a click to a window that ignores mouse events, so a posted one is not taken
+  // there either.
+  CGEventRef cgEvent = theEvent.CGEvent;
+  if (!NSApp.active && !self.window.ignoresMouseEvents && cgEvent) {
+    int64_t sourcePid =
+        CGEventGetIntegerValueField(cgEvent, kCGEventSourceUnixProcessID);
+    if (sourcePid != 0 && sourcePid != getpid()) {
+      return YES;
+    }
+  }
+
   // Enable "click-through" if mouse clicks are accepted in inactive windows.
   return
       [self acceptsMouseEventsOption] > AcceptMouseEvents::kWhenInActiveWindow;
